<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monterey, California</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Monterey is a city on Monterey Bay on the central coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1770 as a presidio and mission, it was the capital of Alta California under Spanish and Mexican rule. On 7 July 1846 Commodore John Sloat raised the American flag there, and California's first constitutional convention met at Monterey in 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monterey-california.jpg" alt="Monterey, California" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Catalinaschool · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santa_Catalina_School,_Monterey,_CA_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Franciscans under Junípero Serra founded a mission at San Diego that year, and <b>Monterey</b>, founded in 1770, later became the capital.</blockquote><a href="/state/alta-california">Alta California</a></li><li><blockquote>On 7 July 1846 Commodore John Sloat raised the American flag at <b>Monterey</b>, and the Stars and Stripes replaced the Bear Flag at Sonoma on 9 July.</blockquote><a href="/state/california-republic">California Republic</a></li></ul></section>
